# [Declare constants]($heading.id('declare-constants'))

Declare module and class constants in the stub:

```php
<?php
namespace MyPHPExt;

/** @var string */
const VERSION = "1.0.0";

class Counter {
    /** @var int */
    public const DEFAULT_STEP = 1;

    /** @var string */
    public const LABEL = "counter";
}
```

The generator emits symbol registration code. At MINIT, phpz calls `register_<name>_symbols` if present. Class registration installs class constants, so each constant needs only one declaration.

After changing the stub, run `zig build gen-stub` and rebuild. The generated code determines constant types and values. Inspect the result through PHP constant access or reflection.
